Z||000000||beer_stud_21||08-01-2001||04:31 PM||||Hey Aus/All,<P>While I was reading the thread about Monkeyman donating a coupe to Aus for his project car I got to thinking.  Seeing as it would cost so much to truck a fiero to california to get shipped to Aus doesn't everyone think it would be cheaper to ship one from Hawaii?  I live about 30 miles from the dock.  I think its only logical to ship a fiero from here instead of trying to get a forum member to ship one to LA.  I've already got a 2000 mile head start.   If Aus can email me I will try to explain better.  Fieros are kind of hard to find around here, but I do have a line on two coupes that are essentually junk yard equivilents in a guys yard about a 1/4 mile from here.   I don't know exactly what condition car Aus wants but I might be able to find something around here.  Aus:  email me at marlinschaefer@mac.com and I will talk to you about it some more.<P>-Marlin<P>edited for moronic speiling errors as usual.. hehe<p>[This message has been edited by beer_stud_21 (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Songman||08-01-2001||07:10 PM||||That's a great idea, Marlin....<P>Not sure if Aus has e-mailed you yet because of time differences but I think he needs the body to be complete but the motor doesn't have to run.<P>Hope you can work something out...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||10
Z||000002||beer_stud_21||08-01-2001||11:13 PM||||*boink™* so Aus spots this thread.||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||08-02-2001||10:38 AM||||Hey thanks for the offer beer_stud_21 but I have a friend that ships container loads of cars and parts out of California often. He is giving me a good deal on shipping. <P>I think I am going to buy one. I asked Pondski if he could check out any cars I find near Los Angeles as if I buy a half decent one I could probably recoupe most of my shipping costs by selling parts off it I don't need.  Pondski has said he would look at any cars I may be interested in. So now I am after 2 half decent Fieros in the LA region. The one I want would actually be goood if it was a V6 auto as I was thinking of converting my 5 speed to auto due to laziness in my fast approaching middle age  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Plus the pedal locations in a right hand driver with a manual transmission  are not really very good. So I will look around the forum, autotrader etc etc.<P>Actually I don't think any ships bound for Australia actually stop in Hawaii anyway (have friends in the merchant navy) So it would have to be shipped to mainland USA then back again. Silly I know but thats the way it works. Although I did have a friend off the USS Chosin bring me some parts from Hawaii...hmmm I wonder if he's got room for a Fiero on the ship  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks again for the offer<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
